At some point I figured out that brown puddings and black puddings
attack different materials.  Wear cloth to protect against one, metal
to protect against the other - basically cloak goes on or comes off.
Hit one with wood, the other with metal - this is when I noticed that
fooproof elven daggers and elven broadswords show up as fireproof
not rustproof.  Learning that made all the difference in the world
when doing melee with rustmonsters.  They went from being
dreaded for the damage they cause to being an easy food source
by swapping armor and weapon when they appear.  Now I no longer
even need to fooproof my stuff.  And I don't even need to worry if
my missile barrage will turn it into dinner before it arrives face to
face.

